.Dd October 1, 2026
.Dt QCOM_FASTRPC 4 aarch64
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qcom_fastrpc
.Nd "Qualcomm FastRPC driver"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the driver as a module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qcom_fastrpc_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver lets programs call code on the compute DSP (CDSP) of Qualcomm
Snapdragon systems-on-chip, home of the NPU, through
.Pa /dev/fastrpc-cdsp ,
with the requests and structures of Linux's FastRPC driver, so that its
user space ports unchanged.
The CDSP must be running, which
.Xr qcom_adsp 4
does; the device appears once the DSP has opened its FastRPC channel over
.Xr qcom_glink 4 .
.Pp
Each open of the device takes a session, one of the DSP's compute context
banks, which translates the DSP's accesses to that program's buffers
through the apps SMMU.
A call's arguments are copied into a buffer mapped through the session,
and its results copied back.
.Pp
The requests supported are
.Dv FASTRPC_IOCTL_INVOKE ,
.Dv FASTRPC_IOCTL_INIT_ATTACH ,
.Dv FASTRPC_IOCTL_INIT_ATTACH_SNS ,
.Dv FASTRPC_IOCTL_INIT_CREATE
and
.Dv FASTRPC_IOCTL_GET_DSP_INFO ,
defined in
.In dev/qcom_fastrpc/fastrpc.h .
.Sh HARDWARE
The
.Nm
driver supports the compute DSP (NSP0) of the Qualcomm Snapdragon 8cx
Gen 3 (SC8280XP), with twelve sessions.
It has been tested on the Radxa Dragon Q8B.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qcom_adsp 4 ,
.Xr qcom_glink 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
driver and this manual page were written by
.An James Kane .
.Sh BUGS
Buffers passed by file descriptor (dma-bufs), maps of memory into the
DSP's processes, static processes and poll mode are not supported, and
their requests fail with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
A call the DSP fails returns
.Er EIO ,
where Linux returns the DSP's result as the request's value.
The module cannot be unloaded.
